# CHIP-8

A portable CHIP-8 interpreter with the original Catch the Dot game built in.
The 64 by 32 virtual screen is scaled onto the selected RGB565 display. Touch
selects one of the sixteen standard CHIP-8 keys. In the game, hold 4 to move
the paddle left or 6 to move it right. Catch the falling dot to increase the
hexadecimal score; a miss resets the score.

The VM supports standard CHIP-8 opcodes, 4 KB of memory, 16 registers, a
16-level call stack, 16 keys, sprite XOR and collision, and 60 Hz timers.
Shifts use Vx, and Fx55/Fx65 leave I unchanged. Sound timer state is
emulated, but this app does not generate audio.
